H9 tsx_amxx.dll -- AMX Mod X's TSX module, built from source for 128 player slots, with a reTS backend
======================================================================================================

What this is
------------

ts\addons\amxmodx\modules\tsx_amxx.dll is AMX Mod X's TSX module (The Specialists' stats and
player natives), built by H9 from TSM\AMXMODX: goldsrc-net/amxmodx branch 64bit at commit
dedff660dff3fa615a96d6ba3890d6000b588ed1, with H9's changes as uncommitted working-tree changes
(AMXMODX\H9-SOURCE.txt). It replaces reTSX, the TSX the reTS release ships: built for 32 slots,
with a reTS backend in no public source.

H9's changes in it
------------------

  modules\ts\tsx\CMisc.h, tsx.h, moduleconfig.cpp, usermsg.cpp
          TSX_MAX_PLAYERS 128: the player table, each player's attackers[] and victims[], and
          TeamInfo's bound cover 128 slots (upstream 32).
  modules\ts\tsx\CMisc.h
          CPlayer::IsBot also takes GetPlayerAuthId "ID_BOT" when the host_ver cvar exists
          (Xash3D FWGS names its bots so); on GoldSrc the answer is unchanged.
  modules\ts\tsx\rets_api.h (new), tsx.h, moduleconfig.cpp, NBase.cpp, usermsg.cpp
          The reTS backend. When the game library exports ReTS_GetInterface (reTS), the natives
          that read or write player state go through that interface (version 6, else 5) rather
          than TS 3.0's member offsets, which reTS's layout does not keep: cash, free slots and
          the move speed that follows them, ammo reserves and stack counts, the status message,
          powerups, slow motion (ts_set_speed, the fake slow motion and slow pause), the bullet
          trail, kung fu and superjump, the powerup pickup, and the thrown knife's thrower in
          the stats. A native whose function a reTS leaves NULL refuses ("Native %s is not
          supported by this reTS"), as reTSX does. rets_api.h is the same file as
          reTS\dlls\rets_api.h. On TS 3.0 every native reads its members by gamedata, as before.
  modules\ts\tsx\NBase.cpp
          A player native given a player not in game refuses with its error instead of going
          on to read him.
  modules\ts\tsx\CMisc.h, Utils.cpp, NBase.cpp, moduleconfig.cpp
          The PPSh-41 of H9's reTS, weapon 39: its name and stats slot (weaponData), the ammo tables
          (caliber 14) and a shot's weapon. 38 stays the thrown knife, which is no game weapon;
          kung fu's own stats slot moves from 39 to 40 and TSMAX_WEAPONS grows by one, so the custom
          weapons start at 41. On TS 3.0's own library the ammo natives refuse a weapon past 37
          ("Weapon %d is not in TS 3.0"), as it has none.
  modules	s	sx\CMisc.h, Utils.cpp, NBase.cpp, moduleconfig.cpp
          The laser rifle of H9's reTS, weapon 40, the same way: its name and stats slot (weaponData), the
          ammo tables (caliber 15) and a shot's weapon. Kung fu's own stats slot moves again, from 40 to 41,
          and TSMAX_WEAPONS grows by one, so the custom weapons start at 42 now.

